	"conclusions": [
		"The core allocates one 64 MiB matrix per invocation and zeros it in finally. Automatic collection timing can leave several old matrices resident.",
		"Plain 64 MiB allocations reproduce the growth without Argon2. All observed Uint32Array instances disappear after final collection.",
		"The WASM oracle already reuses wiped memories through a bounded weak-reference pool. An equivalent TypeScript experiment reduces the sampled process peak substantially.",
		"process.resourceUsage().maxRSS can include memory from before exec in Bun children and should not alone define benchmark-only peak RSS."
	],
